From b2bf7aae759f5d5e94d2ddec3e1c01f0d5b7d50a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:32:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 138/139] panvk: a logic op reads the destination, no forward
 pixel kill

panvk_per_arch(blend_emit_descs)() sets any_dest_read only from the
blend equation, and a logic op keeps its equation at "replace". The draw
then allows forward pixel kill (CSF and JM fragment DCDs, v13 HSR
culling): its fragments may kill the earlier fragments of the same pixel
still in flight, and the blend shader combines the logic op with what is
left in the tile buffer instead of what the earlier draw wrote.

D3D12 feature level 11_1 logic_op check, on every arch (Galaxy A31 v7,
Pixel 6 v9, Pixel 7 v10, Pixel 8 v11): a plain draw writes aaf00fff to an
R8G8B8A8_UINT target cleared to 0, an INVERT draw over it reads back
ffffffff (= ~0, the clear value) instead of 550ff000.

gallium's panfrost_create_blend_state() already sets load_dest for any
logic op. Do the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_blend.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_blend.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_blend.c
index 25ae0212..136efaf8 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_blend.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_blend.c
@@ -377,7 +377,10 @@ panvk_per_arch(blend_emit_descs)(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
        */
       pan_blend_optimize_equation(&rt->equation, rt->format, bs.constants);
 
-      blend_info->any_dest_read |= pan_blend_reads_dest(rt->equation);
+      /* A logic op reads the destination (gallium's load_dest): forward
+       * pixel kill must not drop the fragments it combines with. */
+      blend_info->any_dest_read |=
+         bs.logicop_enable || pan_blend_reads_dest(rt->equation);
 
       if (blend_needs_shader(&bs, i, &ff_blend_constant)) {
          nir_alu_type src0_type = fs_info->bifrost.blend[loc].type;
